	/* ---- Plan tiers ----
	   Laid out by the framework's <Subgrid>: it emits the <ul> and puts
	   `grid-template-rows: subgrid` on it; each tier is authored here as an
	   `<li class="card subgrid-card …">` (Subgrid renders its slot verbatim as
	   of @getvitops/astro 5.0 — it no longer rebuilds children into <li>s), so
	   the three tranches — head, feature list, CTA — snap to shared row lines
	   across all cards regardless of feature count.

	   The variable names are the framework's public contract:
	   --subgrid-cols / --subgrid-row-span / --subgrid-gap / --subgrid-row-gap.
	   They must match exactly — an unrecognised name silently falls back to the
	   pattern's default, and the default row-span is 2 against our 3 tranches,
	   which drops the CTA out of the subgrid and onto its own auto row.

	   --subgrid-gap is BOTH the column gap and the gap between tranches, so it
	   can't be split here; --subgrid-row-gap is extra space once cards wrap.

	   --subgrid-card-rows MUST mirror --subgrid-row-span. `.subgrid-card` (on
	   each <li>, for the position: relative a stretched-link needs) declares
	   its own `grid-row: span var(--subgrid-card-rows, 4)`, same specificity as
	   `.subgrid > *`'s `grid-row: span var(--subgrid-row-span, 2)` and later in
	   the stylesheet — so it wins the cascade, and --subgrid-row-span alone is
	   silently ignored on any element that also carries .subgrid-card. Leaving
	   --subgrid-card-rows at its default (4) here would span each tier across
	   4 row tracks against 3 real tranches, i.e. exactly the "CTA falls out of
	   the subgrid" failure the paragraph above warns about, from the other
	   variable.

	   The <ul> is emitted inside the component, so it sits outside this page's
	   style scope — hence :global(). The <li> cards and everything nested in
	   them are rendered from this file and stay scoped as usual. */
	:global(.pricing-tiers) {
		--subgrid-cols: 3;
		--subgrid-row-span: 3; /* head · feature list · CTA */
		--subgrid-card-rows: 3; /* must match --subgrid-row-span; see above */
		--subgrid-gap: 1.5rem;
		--subgrid-row-gap: 1.5rem; /* extra separation once cards wrap */
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
